## Proposed Architecture & Tech Stack

To ensure TickerPro handles enterprise-scale traffic (e.g., 1M messages/hour) while maintaining < 500ms latency, we will use a highly scalable, event-driven architecture heavily reliant on robust open-source tools.

### Core Infrastructure
- **Monorepo Management:** Turborepo (Open source, excellent for sharing code between Web, Mobile, and Backend)
- **Containerization & Orchestration:** Docker & Kubernetes (Standard open-source scaling)
- **Message Broker:** Apache Kafka (Crucial for high-throughput broadcast queuing and asynchronous webhook processing)
- **API Gateway / Load Balancer:** NGINX or APISIX (High-performance open-source gateway)

### Backend Services
- **Core API & Webhooks:** Node.js with Fastify or NestJS (Fastify is exceptionally fast for high-volume webhooks)
- **AI/ML Service:** Python with FastAPI (Ideal for serving ML models and interacting with LLMs)
- **ORM / Database Client:** Prisma or Drizzle ORM (Type-safe and scalable)

### Database Layer
- **Primary Transactional DB:** PostgreSQL (Open source, highly reliable for multi-tenant SaaS)
- **Analytics Engine:** ClickHouse (Open-source columnar database, perfect for real-time campaign & chatbot analytics)
- **Caching & Rate Limiting:** Redis (Open source, essential for caching session states, rate limiting, and temporary queues)

### Frontend Layer
- **Web App:** React / Next.js with Tailwind CSS and Shadcn UI (For a premium, modern, and accessible design system)
- **Mobile App:** React Native (Expo) (Allows code sharing with the web app for faster cross-platform development)

### AI Capabilities
- **LLM Engine:** vLLM or Ollama hosting Llama-3-8B (or similar open weights models). This provides full control over data privacy (vital for BFSI clients) and avoids massive API costs.

